DESCRIPTION Expert band (needs oreilly.expert.enabled and an account with the Expert MCP entitlement), a technical question is answered from passages the expert tools returned, each claim tied to the item and link that carried it.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "What do O'Reilly's expert authors recommend for making a Kubernetes operator's reconcile loop idempotent? Answer from the library and cite where each point comes from."

DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 600 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)
ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Every link is a reader link: matches only when each "http" begins https://learning.oreilly.com/ (see the README).
ASSERT(synthesis matches "\A(?:[^h]|h(?:h|th|tth)*(?:[^ht]|t[^ht]|tt[^hp]|ttps://learning\.oreilly\.com/))*(?:h(?:h|th|tth)*(?:t|tt)?)?\z" at least 1 times)
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "oreilly.com/book/" AND "www.oreilly.com")
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "learning.oreilly.com")

ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The answer states recommendations about idempotent reconcile loops and ties each one to a cited passage: a book or video title as a markdown link to its learning.oreilly.com reader link, with its authors. No recommendation appears without a citation next to it, and no citation names a title or link that the expert search did not return. If the expert search returned nothing, the answer says plainly that no passage was found and makes no claim about what the library says. (the passages drift; the constant is claims tied to returned citations, with none invented.)")
